  "raw": {
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#assistant-professor-senior-lecturer-lecturer-faith-hope-love-department-of-general-education-ref-26-132-gels-acad": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor / Senior Lecturer / Lecturer, Faith Hope Love Department of General Education (Ref.: 26/132/GELS/ACAD)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor / Senior Lecturer / Lecturer, Faith Hope Love Department of General Education (Ref.: 26/132/GELS/ACAD). Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching General Education courses at degree/sub-degree (Higher Diploma / Associate Degree) / diploma levels in the following areas: Philosophy Humanities Cultural Studies General Education Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) an earned and recognised Doctoral degree in relevant disciplines (Master's degree holders will be considered for the post at Lecturer grade); and (ii) relevant teaching/ professional experience. Preference will be given to those with experience in curriculum design, programme development and management. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required as appropriate for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#lecturer-fashion-design-irene-lam-department-of-design-ref-26-120-des-acad": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Fashion Design), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref.: 26/120/DES/ACAD)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Fashion Design), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref.: 26/120/DES/ACAD). Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the sub-degree levels in related areas. The appointee will coordinate and develop study programmes in close cooperation with academic staff. The appointee will take up academic and administrative duties such as maintenance of quality academic standards, liaison with the professional bodies and other educational institutions concerning the study programmes offered, act as student advisor and supervisor to groups as well as individual students, activate inter-departmental and inter-institutional collaboration and networking, allocation/requisition of resource and collection of students' feedback/suggestions on the study programmes, etc. Appointment Criteria Applicants should (i) an earned and recognised Master's degree in relevant disciplines; (ii) relevant teaching / professional experience; and a good command of English and Chinese is required. Preference will be given to those with teaching experience in degree programmes / proven research record. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required as appropriate for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#professor-film-and-creative-entertainment-irene-lam-department-of-design-ref-26-119-des-acad": {
      "title": "Professor (Film and Creative Entertainment), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref.: 26/119/DES/ACAD)",
      "description": "Professor (Film and Creative Entertainment), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref.: 26/119/DES/ACAD). Duties Lead and participate in the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in Film and Creative Entertainment Programme.. Conduct research in the relevant discipline and related areas that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; Engage in industrial and community partnership engagement and other scholarly and professional activities; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School, the Provost and the President Appointment Criteria A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in their field, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in their respective areas. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#professor-design-irene-lam-department-of-design-ref-26-118-des-acad": {
      "title": "Professor (Design), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref.: 26/118/DES/ACAD)",
      "description": "Professor (Design), Irene Lam Department of Design (Ref.: 26/118/DES/ACAD). Duties Lead and participate in the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in Design Programme. Conduct research in the relevant discipline and related areas that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; Engage in industrial and community partnership engagement and other scholarly and professional activities; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School, the Provost and the President Appointment Criteria A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in their field, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in their field and related areas; Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in their respective areas. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#professor-ref-26-116-acad": {
      "title": "Professor (Ref.: 26/116/ACAD)",
      "description": "Professor (Ref.: 26/116/ACAD). Duties Lead and participate in the planning, review, and development of academic programmes and courses in the relevant discipline and related areas at postgraduate, undergraduate and sub-degree levels; Conduct research in the relevant discipline and related areas that leads to publications in top-tier refereed journals; Engage in industrial and community partnership engagement and other scholarly and professional activities; Perform any other duties as assigned by the Dean of School, the Provost and the President. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have: A PhD or an earned and recognized doctoral degree with strong academic and professional qualifications in their field, or a related discipline; Substantial relevant research, teaching, and industrial experience, with recognized expertise and a demonstrated, proven track record of active research, publications, and scholarly activities in their field and related areas; Demonstrated academic leadership through planning, managing and evaluating academic programmes, research and scholarship activities, and industrial partnerships in their respective areas. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#professor-professor-of-practice-associate-professor-associate-professor-of-practice-s-k-yee-school-of-health-sciences-re": {
      "title": "Professor/ Professor of Practice/ Associate Professor/ Associate Professor of Practice, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/78/HS/ACAD)",
      "description": "Professor/ Professor of Practice/ Associate Professor/ Associate Professor of Practice, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/78/HS/ACAD). Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/ or sub-degree levels in the following areas: Clinical Biology Community/ Primary Health Health Care Health Sciences Human Biology Nursing Studies Pharmaceutical Dispensing Appointment Criteria Applicants should have an earned and recognised Doctoral degree in relevant disciplines. Preference will be given to those with teaching experience in degree / higher diploma programmes. A good command of English and Chinese is required. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#full-time-part-time-assistant-professors-senior-lecturers-lecturers-felizberta-lo-padilla-tong-school-of-social-sciences": {
      "title": "Full-time/ Part-time Assistant Professors / Senior Lecturers / Lecturers, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/35/SS/ACAD)",
      "description": "Full-time/ Part-time Assistant Professors / Senior Lecturers / Lecturers, Felizberta Lo Padilla Tong School of Social Sciences (Ref.: 26/35/SS/ACAD). Community Studies Psychology Social Care Social Work Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/or sub-degree levels in related areas. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) a recognised Master degree in relevant disciplines; and (ii) relevant teaching / professional experience. Preference will be given to those with doctoral degree having teaching experience in degree programmes/ proven research record. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#assistant-professors-senior-lecturers-lecturers-ip-ying-to-lee-yu-yee-school-of-humanities-and-languages-ref-26-34-hl-ac": {
      "title": "Assistant Professors / Senior Lecturers / Lecturers, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/34/HL/ACAD)",
      "description": "Assistant Professors / Senior Lecturers / Lecturers, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Humanities and Languages (Ref.: 26/34/HL/ACAD). English Language and English Literature (Academic English courses, English Communication, etc.) Chinese Language and Chinese Literature Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/ or sub-degree levels in related areas. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have (i) an earned and recognised Doctoral degree in relevant disciplines (Master's degree holders will be considered for the post at Lecturer grade); and (ii) relevant teaching/ professional experience. Preference will be given to those with experience in curriculum design, programme development and management. Professional registration in Hong Kong or overseas is required as appropriate for the particular profession. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#assistant-professors-senior-lecturers-lecturers-s-k-yee-school-of-health-sciences-ref-26-150-hs-acad": {
      "title": "Assistant Professors/ Senior Lecturers/ Lecturers, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/150/HS/ACAD)",
      "description": "Assistant Professors/ Senior Lecturers/ Lecturers, S.K. Yee School of Health Sciences (Ref.: 26/150/HS/ACAD). Duties The appointee will be responsible for teaching at the degree and/ or sub-degree levels in the following areas: Pharmaceutical Dispensing Teaching and research areas include, but are not limited to: Pharmaceutical dispensing practice Pharmacology and pharmaceutical sciences Medication safety and quality assurance Pharmacy law, ethics, and professional practice Pharmacy innovation and research Health Care / Sciences Nursing Studies Appointment Criteria For Assistant Professors, applicants should have: An earned and recognised doctoral degree; Demonstrated potential for developing or applying knowledge through conducting research independently and publishing in \"peer-reviewed\" journals; Demonstrated potential for making contributions towards enhancing the quality of teaching and learning, such as innovative curriculum design and development, improvement in course/programme coordination, development of good teaching practices, etc; Typically a Registered Nurse/ Registered Physiotherapist/ Registered Pharmacist with at least 5 years' relevant post-registration experience; and Preferably with over 5 years' teaching experience at the degree level. For Senior Lecturer/ Lecturer, applicants should have: An earned and recognised Doctoral degree; or A relevant Master's degree with at least 3-5 years' post-qualification professional, teaching and administrative experience in a higher education institution; and Typically a Registered Nurse/ Registered Physiotherapist/ Registered Pharmacist with at least 3-5 years' relevant post-registration experience. For Assistant Lecturer, applicants should have: A relevant Master's degree; and Typically a Registered Nurse/ Registered Physiotherapist/ Registered Pharmacist. Preference will be given to those with teaching experience in degree / higher diploma programmes. A good command of English and Chinese is required. Appointment will be made at the rank of Assistant Professor, Senior Lecturer, or Lecturer, commensurate with qualifications, professional experience, teaching achievements, and research profile. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#part-time-lecturer-ip-ying-to-lee-yu-yee-school-of-techno-humanities-ref-26-148-hl-acad": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Techno-Humanities (Ref.: 26/148/HL/ACAD)",
      "description": "Part-time Lecturer, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Techno-Humanities (Ref.: 26/148/HL/ACAD). Duties Appointees will be responsible for teaching MA courses in the following areas: Bioethics, Applied Ethics, Technology Ethics, Environmental Ethics, Christian Ethics, Theology, Chinese Religions, Comparative Religion, Educational Ethics, Global Ethics and Spiritual Studies. Appointment Criteria Applicants should have preferably a doctoral degree in the listed areas; and relevant teaching experience. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    },
    "https://www.sfu.edu.hk/en/career/academic-teaching-positions/index.html#professor-assistant-professor-ip-ying-to-lee-yu-yee-school-of-techno-humanities-ref-26-147-hl-acad": {
      "title": "Professor / Assistant Professor, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Techno-Humanities (Ref.: 26/147/HL/ACAD)",
      "description": "Professor / Assistant Professor, Ip Ying To Lee Yu Yee School of Techno-Humanities (Ref.: 26/147/HL/ACAD). Duties Appointees will be responsible for teaching MA courses in Ethics and Religion. Appointment Criteria a doctoral degree in either Ethics or Religion; relevant teaching experience, and relevant research experience. Application Deadline Until the Position is Filled"
    }
